A||||7||Jasons85GT||Troubled Fiero ...(Any suggestions?)||||9||
Z||000000||Jasons85GT||10-28-2001||11:52 AM||||Ok, I need some help. Heres what happened...<P>Day 1: Took her out for a spin, ran great. Pulled up to a stop light, sat for like 10 sec, then she died. Started right back up, but kept acting like it wanted to shut off again unless I kept gassing it. After about 2-3 min, it ran fine again. On the way home, the check engine light came on, but no more stalling.  <P>Day 2: Took it back out again. Ran fine. Then after about 30 min of driving, the RPMs started dipping down like it wanted to die again. Came to a stop, stalled. Started right back up, check engine light comes on, but runs fine again. <P>Day 3: Started it up. After it warmed up a little, i noticed it had an unsteady, low idle. About 550-700, up and down. After a while of driving, it dies again. <P>Conclusion: I dont know what it is! I've replaced O2 sensor, control module, coil, fuel filter...ect. I dont have a code reader either.(need to get one) Any ideas? Any replies or suggestions are appreciated! Thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||10-28-2001||12:01 PM||||A code reader is just a bent paper clip. Your Haynes manual gives the whole procedure and the meanings of the codes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||10-28-2001||05:58 PM||||Invest in a paper clip, like Phil says.  Try removing/cleaning the idle air control (IAC) motor, and the passages in the throttle body.  <P>A couple things that affect idle speed are: Air supply (IAC mentioned above), and ignition timing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||samoht||10-28-2001||05:58 PM||||Sounds like ICV .. but get the hayes and a paper clip first.. I am sure the book will pay for itself <P><BR>85gt3.2||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-28-2001||06:26 PM||||EGR system. ||||reg||4
Z||000005||Sootah||10-28-2001||06:39 PM||||Gremlins.||||reg||12
